                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I honestly think it's a pretty good game. I mean...I went out of my way to beat it as all four of the playable characters, that should tell you everything.\n\nBasically everything that I already loved about the first game was improved tenfold with this second entry, like the spritework, the art style, the gameplay, and the OST (Yes, I like FP2's OST, sue me). That's not to say I don't still like the first game, heck yeah I still love it, but FP2, though it was a bit rocky for me at first, I've grown to absolutely love it, and I feel like there's something FP2 does for me that just makes it even better for me to play.\n\nThe only lowpoints for me were some aspects of the story, as well as two of the levels. The story I felt had a bit too many subplots that distracted from the main conflict, and subsequently made Merga feel like less of a threat than she really was, but this was a really minor issue in the grand scheme of things.\n\nThe other thing I didn't like were two of the levels. Ancestral Forge, and Clockwork Arboretum. You've already heard people drone on about Ancestral Forge so I don't even feel like I need to explain it, and Clockwork Arboretum was just a little boring with the whole elevator mechanic, which made the level feel really slow and tedious.\n\nBut again, for me, these were just some minor blemishes on an otherwise perfect game for me. I'd say this game, at the very least, gets an A- from me.",
